Probably not worth debating, but I don't consider nethack a puzzle game, 
because the main hardship isn't figuring it out.  Yes, it is certainly 
harder if one is unspoiled, so I agree that there is some puzzle element, 
but even Marvin doesn't ascend every time, so it's clearly not just about 
puzzles.  
However, we're probably just defining puzzle games differently.  
Regardless, what I was saying is what David Ploog has now said better in a 
different place on this thread.  I don't think Sokoban fits very well with 
the rest of the game.  Sure one can avoid Sokoban, I usually do.  But the 
fact is, it doesn't really fit with the whole dungeon idea and reminds me a 
lot more of Zelda than anything else, because it's non-random and tedious.  
I do agree that a randomized Sokoban would be much more in style and that 
would be nice, but still viable way to do the puzzle without a lot of rock 
pushing.  Yeah, in theory I could break most of the rocks and use scrolls, 
but maxed negative luck sounds most of impossible to handle.  (Note that I 
carefully didn't say it was totally impossible.)
Earlier this preference was compared to a dislike of pets and I feel this 
is rather different.  I also happen to dislike pets and have never ascended 
a character that wasn't petless (though if I ever finish my bored 
extinctionist it won't be petless,) but that is more of a conduct than a 
different path.  Sure it takes somewhat different strategies to ascend, but 
it's mainly the same cup of tea.  However, skipping Sokoban generally just 
means more polypiling, wishing or searching.  
*shrug* Maybe this doesn't make sense, so if not ignore me ;).


